  "hypothesis": "H88-UNIQ-20261025: Blind-basin off-catalogue fault segments are more likely where (a) the radiometric K/Th ratio is anomalously high (GeoDAWN hydrothermal K enrichment / Th depletion), (b) the RTP magnetic field shows a local demagnetization trough (magnetite destruction, training_features band 2), and (c) the DEM shows a subtle topographic lineament (curvature contrast, bands 12 and 19). Dot emission is weighted by the conjunction surface within 3-25 px of catalogue faults (proximal halo for holdout recovery) plus a true blind-zone allocation (>26 px) for novelty. Differs from prior lanes that use distance-alone, lattice placement, or single-physics emission.",
